CONCLUSION: vkms card2 is a seat device (tagged master-of-seat).
systemd-logind grants the ACTIVE session user (emzmo on seat0) an ACL
(user:emzmo:rw-) AND the ability to acquire DRM master even while
Hyprland holds it, via the seat's master-of-seat coordination.
This is why test_sim_display_acquires_vkms + test_sigterm_releases_master
PASS UNPRIVILEGED (uid 1000) on this bench without sudo.
The ADR-010 narrative ('unprivileged EACCES on tty3') was true for the
prior session's context (idle tty3, not the active seat0 session) but is
NOT a general property — it depends on which session is Active on seat0.
The fix session's tests passed for the SAME reason mine do now: active
seat0 session + logind ACL, NOT undocumented root privilege.
